WEBVTT

00:11.030 --> 00:12.870
I never had a mother.

00:14.010 --> 00:17.550
My father was a doctor who treated the poor and sickly.

00:20.600 --> 00:23.930
When I was four, he brought me with him to this country.

00:26.170 --> 00:28.300
I was always alone.

00:29.270 --> 00:34.270
People would get killed each and every day in gunfights.

00:35.930 --> 00:41.670
The only relief I had was a manga that a Japanese volunteer had brought.

00:42.420 --> 00:48.750
The manga called: "School Revolution" was something I read until it was all worn and tattered.

00:52.470 --> 01:00.090
Eventually, my father's oversea work term ended and he brought me back to my birthplace.

01:01.260 --> 01:06.190
In this country, we didn't have to worry about running out of drinking water.

01:07.500 --> 01:09.250
Like in a place out of a dream.

01:23.480 --> 01:24.950
Want to play together?

01:30.920 --> 01:31.880
Let's play!

01:35.310 --> 01:36.440
What's your name?

01:36.440 --> 01:37.300
I'm Aya.

01:44.470 --> 01:45.520
He was...

01:46.410 --> 01:49.490
My first friend.

02:09.740 --> 02:11.420
Well then, I'll see you tomorrow.

02:11.420 --> 02:12.980
Yeah, see you tomorrow.

02:18.660 --> 02:19.830
Tomorrow...

02:44.470 --> 02:45.990
Aya!

03:04.430 --> 03:05.640
It's cold.

03:35.260 --> 03:42.100
Presented By Refrain Subs!

03:45.770 --> 03:51.650
Since being alone was tough, the two of us held hands.

03:52.150 --> 03:58.160
The two of us were lonely, so we all stood in a circle and joined hands.

03:58.120 --> 04:06.370
I'm sure that's where we will gather our strength.

04:06.290 --> 04:11.340
Enough to stand up to any dream.

04:11.210 --> 04:13.970
Fly high towards the sky,

04:13.630 --> 04:18.140
Kick off the ground and send your voice to the heavens,

04:17.840 --> 04:23.180
Until you overcome those painful days.

04:22.970 --> 04:28.310
I'll never forget your voice, and I'll never forget your tears.

04:24.980 --> 04:25.020
The First Annual Make Kyousuke Chuckle Championships

04:27.940 --> 04:35.280
The future that we call "hope" begins now.

04:35.030 --> 04:46.080
Your feet will continue to step onward, even when the time of grief comes.

05:01.520 --> 05:05.170
I was repeating the same scene all over again.

05:05.270 --> 05:06.480
Um...

05:06.480 --> 05:07.980
I'm Naoe.

05:07.980 --> 05:09.720
You dropped this.

05:10.390 --> 05:13.220
Just how many times have I met Riki-kun now?

05:16.120 --> 05:17.140
Treasure?

05:17.490 --> 05:21.110
Is there gold or something like that buried under this school?

05:24.390 --> 05:30.620
Riki-kun doesn't know that we have repeated the same adventure many times.

05:36.050 --> 05:38.160
I'm always worried...

05:38.850 --> 05:42.040
Will Riki-kun ever fall in love with me again?

05:43.490 --> 05:44.090
Huh?

05:44.090 --> 05:48.500
Stop fooling around and pay attention!

05:49.480 --> 05:50.450
And...

05:50.870 --> 05:51.910
Saya!

05:56.830 --> 06:00.480
I would die over and over again.

06:07.900 --> 06:11.870
Am I an idiot?!

06:11.870 --> 06:14.740
How many times has it been now?

06:14.740 --> 06:17.680
What the hell am I doing?

06:23.590 --> 06:25.250
You've made it here again?

06:25.250 --> 06:27.210
How long do you intend to keep repeating this?

06:27.210 --> 06:29.040
This is such a crappy game.

06:29.040 --> 06:30.760
Die, you bastard!

06:37.160 --> 06:38.570
It's hopeless.

06:38.570 --> 06:41.010
I'm the game master of this world.

06:41.010 --> 06:42.480
You can't possibly win.

06:43.190 --> 06:46.610
You're an anomaly that shouldn't be here.

06:47.160 --> 06:48.610
I know that.

06:48.610 --> 06:50.860
I'm an irregular in this world.

06:50.860 --> 06:53.200
I have to disappear someday.

06:53.580 --> 06:58.690
Fine then, the next game over will be my last.

06:58.690 --> 07:01.930
I'll leave after that, so just let me repeat it one more time...

07:02.440 --> 07:03.500
Let me obtain it.

07:06.220 --> 07:08.710
One round is more than enough.

07:17.320 --> 07:18.680
That's right.

07:18.680 --> 07:20.530
This is the last game.

07:20.530 --> 07:22.140
No more replays after this.

07:22.690 --> 07:24.330
This will be the end.

07:26.430 --> 07:28.950
These will be the final moments I get to spend with Riki-kun.

07:30.000 --> 07:33.060
Spending all these fun times with him...

07:33.770 --> 07:35.160
This is more than...

07:37.060 --> 07:39.070
What's wrong, Saya?

07:39.070 --> 07:41.290
Why are you just calling me "Saya"?

07:42.060 --> 07:43.830
I don't know when,

07:43.830 --> 07:47.750
but I feel like I used to call you that a long time ago.

07:53.410 --> 07:55.190
Why are you crying?

07:55.190 --> 07:56.760
I'm not crying.

07:57.730 --> 07:59.010
Saya.

07:59.700 --> 08:00.660
I love you.

08:04.160 --> 08:06.390
Probably, since long ago.

08:23.960 --> 08:25.080
Riki-kun...

08:25.080 --> 08:25.790
What is it?

08:27.120 --> 08:28.610
Just calling you.

08:45.010 --> 08:48.730
I guess we're finally getting close to the treasure.

08:50.960 --> 08:53.900
Hey, Saya, what exactly is the treasure?

08:54.270 --> 08:55.680
I wonder...

08:55.680 --> 08:57.260
How does a time machine sound?

08:57.260 --> 08:58.890
Time machine, huh?

09:00.600 --> 09:01.980
Mysterious, isn't it?

09:01.980 --> 09:04.750
I was thinking the same thing.

09:04.750 --> 09:09.870
If that were the case, wouldn't it be great to travel back to when we were kids?

09:09.870 --> 09:11.540
And do everything over again.

09:12.130 --> 09:13.750
Starting from our childhood.

09:15.900 --> 09:17.760
Hey, if...

09:17.760 --> 09:18.560
Yes?

09:18.560 --> 09:21.650
If we meet again one day...

09:22.300 --> 09:24.430
I'll ask you out on a date, okay?

09:24.710 --> 09:27.040
Not one day. We will as soon as we can.

09:27.040 --> 09:28.650
We'll spend some peaceful time together.

09:28.910 --> 09:32.050
Without any traps or gunfights.

09:32.050 --> 09:33.650
There will only be sunshine...

09:33.970 --> 09:36.060
...and the sound of our laughter.

09:42.780 --> 09:46.450
A-All right, let’s cut the talk and get moving.

09:46.720 --> 09:48.470
The final obstacle awaits us.

09:48.470 --> 09:50.110
The final obstacle?

09:50.110 --> 09:52.210
He has to be defeated.

09:53.300 --> 09:56.980
Riki-kun, could I ask you to be my trump card?

10:17.070 --> 10:18.490
This is the end.

10:19.560 --> 10:24.520
Or so I'd like to say, but to think you'd come up with such a cheap trick...

10:26.490 --> 10:27.960
A decoy plan, huh?

10:27.960 --> 10:29.960
Did you really think you could fool me?

10:31.800 --> 10:34.040
You lose, Tokikaze Shun!

10:34.040 --> 10:35.710
Oh, why's that?

10:35.710 --> 10:38.460
You can't possibly shoot me with Riki-kun in the middle.

10:38.460 --> 10:42.220
Even if you change your position, I will react to it.

10:42.640 --> 10:45.600
My reflexes are more than enough for that.

10:45.600 --> 10:49.480
So basically, you're saying he's not a decoy, but your shield instead?

10:49.480 --> 10:50.260
That's right.

10:50.260 --> 10:53.870
What makes you think I won't shoot your partner?

10:54.440 --> 10:56.610
I've dug up my fair share of intelligence, you know.

10:57.090 --> 10:59.570
And I know you can't shoot Riki-kun.

10:59.570 --> 11:01.860
Then bring it on.

11:02.870 --> 11:04.920
I should just shoot him.

11:05.570 --> 11:08.120
But he's not a shadow.

11:08.470 --> 11:10.400
He's a living human being.

11:10.400 --> 11:13.630
Don't worry, Riki-kun, he can't die!

11:21.660 --> 11:23.550
Three gunshots...

11:23.550 --> 11:27.260
All three were fired at the same time.

11:27.260 --> 11:29.060
Saya, are you okay?

11:29.060 --> 11:29.910
Saya!

11:29.910 --> 11:31.200
I'm fine.

11:31.200 --> 11:32.520
Did you get hit?

11:32.520 --> 11:33.890
It's just a scratch.

11:33.890 --> 11:36.580
It's no big deal. Are you hurt?

11:36.580 --> 11:38.140
I'm fine.

11:38.140 --> 11:38.940
What about him?

11:43.160 --> 11:45.590
We've finally won.

11:47.740 --> 11:51.290
The bullet hit him in the shoulder.

11:51.960 --> 11:53.790
He's not dead.

11:53.790 --> 11:56.540
He'll get up when he recovers.

11:56.540 --> 11:58.180
What do we do now?

11:58.180 --> 12:00.770
The treasure is on the lowest level, how do we—

12:00.770 --> 12:03.750
You'll find an elevator that takes you there up ahead.

12:03.750 --> 12:05.510
Why, thank you.

12:05.510 --> 12:07.910
Wait! It might be a trap.

12:08.740 --> 12:09.930
It's all right.

12:09.930 --> 12:12.280
This is the same guy you were fighting against earlier.

12:12.280 --> 12:14.140
There are no traps or tricks left.

12:14.470 --> 12:18.880
Defeating me has earned her the right to the treasure.

12:19.480 --> 12:21.480
That's how it works, Riki-kun.

12:23.490 --> 12:26.780
Those are the rules of this world.

12:47.550 --> 12:49.150
We've finally made it, huh?

12:49.150 --> 12:52.660
The treasure is on the lowest level, the 60th basement floor.

12:52.660 --> 12:54.390
60th basement floor?

13:24.440 --> 13:27.140
The treasure is in there, isn't it?

13:28.470 --> 13:29.340
Yep.

13:30.210 --> 13:34.790
I expected something more grand than this.

13:42.420 --> 13:43.840
I'm going in.

14:26.220 --> 14:27.510
Saya?

14:34.100 --> 14:35.490
What's wrong?

14:35.490 --> 14:36.610
Are you hurt?

14:36.610 --> 14:37.870
Saya?

14:37.870 --> 14:39.740
Hey, can you hear me?

14:39.740 --> 14:41.330
What happened?

14:41.830 --> 14:43.880
Please respond!

14:43.880 --> 14:44.790
Riki-kun.

14:45.120 --> 14:47.050
I need you to calm down.

14:47.400 --> 14:49.920
The treasure was a bioweapon.

14:50.370 --> 14:52.630
Bioweapon?

14:52.630 --> 14:54.430
So this is farewell.

14:56.150 --> 14:57.640
No!

14:57.950 --> 14:59.940
I don't understand!

14:59.940 --> 15:01.510
What the hell are you talking about?

15:01.510 --> 15:03.600
I'm coming in as well!

15:05.450 --> 15:06.800
Get out here!

15:06.800 --> 15:09.240
Explain to me what happened!

15:09.240 --> 15:11.450
Hey, Saya-san!

15:11.450 --> 15:12.570
Hey!

15:23.340 --> 15:24.720
Riki-kun...

15:24.720 --> 15:27.540
The route where you meet me leads to a bad end.

15:29.250 --> 15:31.950
There's no good end to be found here.

15:31.950 --> 15:35.300
What are you talking about? What do you mean by <i>end?</i>

15:35.300 --> 15:38.140
Just once more, huh?

15:39.160 --> 15:43.350
It seems you've finally come to understand the truth.

15:43.830 --> 15:50.260
Tokido Saya is a character that appears in my favorite manga, "School Revolution."

15:46.860 --> 15:46.900
She totally doesn't seem like that...

15:47.820 --> 15:47.860
This voice... I've heard it before.

15:47.820 --> 15:47.860
Well, I guess you'll learn
your lesson soon.

15:47.860 --> 15:48.410
I told you to stay
out of this...

15:47.860 --> 15:47.900
I told you to stay
out of this...

15:48.020 --> 15:48.070
Don't tell me
I didn't warn you.

15:51.030 --> 15:55.220
But without my realizing it, the soul of a girl who died in an accident...

15:55.220 --> 15:57.530
wandered into this world

15:57.530 --> 16:01.020
and started acting as Tokido Saya.

16:02.840 --> 16:04.230
I knew that...

16:04.230 --> 16:07.180
I knew that I shouldn't be here.

16:07.180 --> 16:09.800
That I would have to disappear one day.

16:09.800 --> 16:10.710
That's why...

16:11.920 --> 16:13.930
I've been trying so hard all this time!

16:13.990 --> 16:17.230
I hadn't even experienced my first love yet!

16:17.230 --> 16:20.260
I died without knowing what it feels like.

16:21.360 --> 16:24.230
The youth I always wanted to experience was here...

16:25.680 --> 16:28.000
In this gentle world.

16:29.800 --> 16:32.900
I know that everyone here is kind.

16:33.510 --> 16:34.740
Even you are kind.

16:34.740 --> 16:38.140
If you really wanted to, you could've gotten rid of me at any time.

16:39.800 --> 16:42.800
But instead, you waited until I was satisfied.

16:44.240 --> 16:46.190
Don't you worry.

16:46.190 --> 16:48.270
I'll disappear on my own volition.

16:48.830 --> 16:50.340
How do you plan to do that?

16:50.700 --> 16:52.650
You're the game master.

16:52.650 --> 16:56.240
So you can turn the treasure into whatever you want, can't you?

16:56.240 --> 16:57.500
Yes.

16:57.500 --> 17:01.760
That's because the treasure hasn't even been revealed in the manga yet.

17:02.350 --> 17:04.640
Make the treasure a bioweapon.

17:05.180 --> 17:10.470
That way, I can at least complete my adventure...

17:11.130 --> 17:13.880
...before disappearing from this world.

17:13.880 --> 17:15.990
Is that really okay with you?

17:19.290 --> 17:21.290
I'm sorry, Riki-kun.

17:22.370 --> 17:24.870
Thank you for hanging out with me.

17:26.240 --> 17:28.780
Thank you for all this time.

17:31.500 --> 17:33.690
Thank you for loving me.

17:35.600 --> 17:39.630
This is how it ends in this world.

17:42.960 --> 17:43.790
Huh?

17:45.060 --> 17:46.890
I told myself I wouldn't cry.

17:49.700 --> 17:54.690
Riki-kun, everyone, and this world...

17:57.750 --> 17:59.330
I've come to truly love them both.

17:59.900 --> 18:04.260
I've spent time with Riki-kun in this gentle world.

18:05.040 --> 18:10.690
I was able to enjoy my youth as much as I wanted with Riki-kun.

18:11.680 --> 18:14.200
Thank you, Riki-kun.

18:14.800 --> 18:16.950
Time should just freeze here.

18:16.950 --> 18:19.630
At this moment where Saya is present.

18:19.630 --> 18:23.300
I wish it could stay like this forever and ever.

18:23.300 --> 18:24.570
I'm Tokido.

18:24.570 --> 18:26.080
I'm Naoe.

18:26.080 --> 18:27.810
You dropped this.

18:28.280 --> 18:29.590
Naoe-kun, huh?

18:29.590 --> 18:30.770
Thanks a lot.

18:30.770 --> 18:33.020
Yeah, yeah... I fell asleep.

18:33.020 --> 18:34.760
The Saya that I love.

18:34.760 --> 18:38.150
I slept like a rock, just as you thought.

18:38.150 --> 18:39.530
My beloved Saya.

18:39.530 --> 18:42.450
All right! I got it!

18:42.710 --> 18:43.990
You're lying. You saw!

18:43.990 --> 18:45.410
I-I didn't see...

18:45.410 --> 18:46.360
that much.

18:46.360 --> 18:48.450
"That much"? What do you mean by that?!

18:49.260 --> 18:50.780
Please close your eyes.

18:51.480 --> 18:52.620
Why?

18:53.990 --> 18:58.710
Because even if we're on a battlefield, you're supposed to close them.

18:59.830 --> 19:02.690
If I'm supposed to... then I guess I will.

19:10.340 --> 19:11.840
Somehow, for us...

19:13.020 --> 19:14.250
This moment...

19:15.330 --> 19:17.470
Please, just let us stay like this forever.

19:31.210 --> 19:32.440
Saya...

19:33.260 --> 19:34.730
I don't know when...

19:35.590 --> 19:39.740
but I feel like I used to call you that a long time ago.

19:51.060 --> 19:59.170
The fever of my heart was gradually taken

19:54.980 --> 19:56.520
Yo, are you awake?

19:59.200 --> 20:00.830
Hey, Kyousuke...

20:01.100 --> 20:10.860
By a coldness that was like snow

20:01.400 --> 20:04.760
I had an important partner.

20:04.760 --> 20:05.660
Yeah.

20:06.120 --> 20:08.080
But then I lost her.

20:08.920 --> 20:09.850
Is that so?

20:10.660 --> 20:16.160
I heard the Darkness Executives were overconfident.

20:11.560 --> 20:21.400
I knew everything, I lost everything

20:18.440 --> 20:24.650
And that the spy called Tokido Saya escaped successfully.

20:21.420 --> 20:29.960
But that's okay, because that's what came from trying to grasp something

20:25.450 --> 20:26.820
Escaped?

20:30.340 --> 20:33.320
Riki, it was gone.

20:30.750 --> 20:35.420
The first was brightness

20:34.440 --> 20:38.620
The time machine that the Darkness Executives were guarding.

20:35.490 --> 20:40.900
The second was warmth

20:40.010 --> 20:43.110
Would you believe me if I said so?

20:40.820 --> 20:50.890
Anything more would just be selfish

20:47.570 --> 20:51.460
There were traces of someone using it to get away.

20:51.190 --> 21:01.110
Thank you for the radiance inside of kindness

20:57.120 --> 21:01.140
We may meet again some day.

21:01.420 --> 21:11.960
Just that is more than enough for me

21:09.990 --> 21:11.970
I'm alive...

21:12.260 --> 21:17.130
Spring ends

21:13.720 --> 21:15.430
How is that possible?

21:16.180 --> 21:18.820
Huh? I have such small hands.

21:17.350 --> 21:24.780
And the long dream passes

21:19.780 --> 21:21.650
Are you awake, Aya?

21:24.990 --> 21:29.800
I truly wanted to be with everyone

21:27.510 --> 21:28.590
How are you doing?

21:28.590 --> 21:30.390
Did you have a dream?

21:30.120 --> 21:40.260
In the summer and fall too

21:32.520 --> 21:35.300
Yeah. It was a really long dream.

21:35.880 --> 21:40.250
We went into an underground labyrinth and got into gunfights.

21:40.600 --> 21:45.680
I had a partner, and he loved me.

21:45.680 --> 21:47.420
I loved him as well.

21:48.610 --> 21:50.090
I really loved him.

21:50.400 --> 21:52.850
Aya's first love, huh?

21:54.350 --> 21:56.820
He'll come again.

21:56.820 --> 21:59.930
The boy who plays with you every day since you came back.

22:00.200 --> 22:05.000
Thank you, for all of

22:00.580 --> 22:04.540
The way I see it, the boy likes you.

22:05.230 --> 22:10.060
Thank you, the memories

22:05.570 --> 22:07.570
All right, let's get moving!

22:10.370 --> 22:20.380
Anything more would just be selfish

22:10.570 --> 22:15.170
Let's play, Riki-kun!

22:20.570 --> 22:30.700
Thank you for the radiance inside of all of you

22:30.740 --> 22:42.580
Just receiving it is more than enough for me

23:25.250 --> 23:30.420
Episode 4

23:25.250 --> 23:30.420
Sometime, Somewhere...

23:31.090 --> 23:41.070
Episode 5

23:31.090 --> 23:41.070
Sasami Turns Into a Cat

23:32.180 --> 23:33.320
What's the meaning of this?

23:33.320 --> 23:35.870
You're telling me, I, Sasasegawa Sasami, turned into a cat?

23:35.870 --> 23:38.040
Why not? Zazazegawa Zazam—

23:38.040 --> 23:39.870
There is still a secret in this world.
